    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `membershipNumber` for owners, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration date's year.\n\nChanges, each kept in its natural place:\n\n1. **`MembershipNumberGenerator`** (new service component) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class that formats the membership number from a customer code and registration date, mirroring the existing `CustomerCodeGenerator`.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field (mapped to a new `membership_number` column) with its getter/setter.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 injected the generator and assigned the membership number for new owners, right after the existing customer-code assignment (so `customerCode` is already set; `registrationDate` is already defaulted by the controller).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so it's mapped into the DTO (via MapStruct's by-name mapping) and returned by the REST API.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` (which asserts `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY` equals `membershipNumber`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
